  "final_text": "All four steps are done.\n\n1. **Data view:** \"Kibana Sample Data Flights\" covers the index `kibana_sample_data_flights`, and its time field is `timestamp`. Other fields include `Carrier`, `Cancelled` (true/false), `Origin`, `Dest`, `AvgTicketPrice`, `FlightDelayMin` and `DistanceKilometers`.\n2. **Dashboard:** I created \"S4-6ea86b59 Flights\" (id `s4-6ea86b59-flights-0bde79cb7b5e`) with exactly two panels:\n   - **Flights over time:** a line chart counting flights per time interval.\n   - **Carrier panel:** a bar chart counting flights for each of the top 10 carriers.\n3. **Alert rule:** I created \"S4-6ea86b59 Cancelled flights\" (id `d847fcb9-ee0b-4346-ae94-91c12d999bb2`). Every minute it counts flights in `kibana_sample_data_flights` where `Cancelled` is true over the last 5 minutes (by `timestamp`), and fires when the count is above 10. It was created already enabled, so it didn't need to be switched on.\n4. **Edit and check:** I set the carrier panel's title to \"Flights by carrier\". I had already used that title when I created the panel, so the edit didn't change anything. When I read the rule back, it showed `enabled: true` and status `ok`.\n\nTIME_FIELD: timestamp\nRULE_ENABLED: yes",
